 Ecology 
{{Unreferenced section|date=April 2026}}
Brugmansia versicolor is a hermaphrodite that reproduces perennially. It has long, narrow, fusiform berries that are up to {{convert|21|cm|abbr=on}} in length. Brugmansia reproduces by the production of seeds. The major pollinators are thought to be various species of insects, though this has yet to be proven.
